[2026-03-05T19:31:02.285Z] @claude:
Fix cycle 4 interrupted: dispatch worker agent killed its own host daemon while debugging E2E test failures.

The agent was trying to manually start a daemon to test against fixture data after E2E tests showed 'Failed to fetch' errors. Running kspec serve (stop/start/restart) from a dispatch worker kills the global daemon at ~/.config/kspec/daemon.pid, which is the same daemon hosting the dispatch engine. No env guard exists to prevent this.

WIP commit (b06bc63ab) contains partial but untested changes:
- Added type field to daemon task list/detail API responses
- Fixed todo rendering to use actual schema fields (done/text vs status/content)
- Serialized vcs_refs objects to string format for frontend
- Enriched E2E fixtures with full AC-3 required fields
- Expanded AC-3 test to verify type, deps, todos, automation, VCS, plan, session
- Fixed constants.ts for same-origin API in production builds
- Fixed hardcoded localhost:3456 in AC-5 test

Root cause of E2E failures likely: fixture data schema mismatch (agent used wrong todo/vcs_refs shapes initially, then fixed but daemon was killed before re-testing).

Created separate task for dispatch daemon self-protection guard.
